    "title": "pandas.DataFrame.dtypes — pandas 2.2.3 documentation",
    "status": 200,
    "markdown": "# pandas.DataFrame.dtypes#\n\n- \n*property* DataFrame.dtypes[source]#\n- Return the dtypes in the DataFrame. This returns a Series with the data type of each column. The result’s index is the original DataFrame’s columns. Columns with mixed types are stored with the `object` dtype. See\nthe User Guide for more.\n  - Returns:\n    - pandas.Series\n    - The data type of each column.\n Examples >>> df = pd.DataFrame({'float': [1.0], ... 'int': [1], ... 'datetime': [pd.Timestamp('20180310')], ... 'string': ['foo']}) >>> df.dtypes float float64 int int64 datetime datetime64[ns] string object dtype: object",
    "markdown_length": 600,
